-- What the Hours of Work and Rest Law asks for a day spent escorting pupils
-- (MMS-678): the measure every instrument that pays escorting in activity
-- units or substitution hours is held against, written once, from the
-- law's own sections (l4/laws/hours-of-work-law.l4). It holds no
-- assertion; its tests, l4/tests/escort-day-tests.l4, and each
-- instrument's tests file hold what was checked.
--
-- The reading it applies is convention instruments.hours-law-teaching, a
-- pick for the lawyer: the law reaches a teacher escorting pupils, and the
-- hours he is required with them outside the institution are working hours
-- (§1). Whether the hours of a night away, when the pupils sleep and he
-- answers for them, are working hours too is the question that convention
-- puts to the lawyer, so a night away is measured both ways. An hour of the
-- regular wage (§18) is measured against the month by convention
-- instruments.regular-hour-wage: the hours of the full position the
-- instrument sets, and, as the bound most generous to the employer, the
-- 195 hours of a month of §3's longest week.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT hours_of_work_law

§ `יום ליווי תלמידים מול חוק שעות עבודה ומנוחה`

§§ `יום ליווי`

-- A day at the work's disposal from one hour to another, less §20's least
-- break, is §1's working hours; what passes §2's day — seven hours where two
-- or more of them fall between 22:00 and 06:00 — is overtime.
GIVEN `from hour` IS A NUMBER, `to hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the working hours of an escort day` `from hour` `to hour` IS
    `working hours section 1 of the Hours of Work and Rest Law counts`
        (`to hour` MINUS `from hour`)
        (`the least break section 20 asks, in hours` (`to hour` MINUS `from hour`) FALSE)

GIVEN `from hour` IS A NUMBER, `to hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the overtime of an escort day` `from hour` `to hour` IS
    max 0 (`the working hours of an escort day` `from hour` `to hour`
               MINUS `the longest working day section 2 allows`
                         (`night work as section 1 of the Hours of Work and Rest Law means` (max 0 (`to hour` MINUS 22))))

-- §16 on that overtime, in hours of the regular wage.
GIVEN `from hour` IS A NUMBER, `to hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours section 16 asks for an escort day` `from hour` `to hour` IS
    `regular hours' pay section 16 asks for a day's overtime` (`the overtime of an escort day` `from hour` `to hour`)

-- On a day the salary does not pay for — his free day — the law's regular
-- hours are owed too: the working hours up to §2's day at the regular wage,
-- and §16 on the rest.
GIVEN `from hour` IS A NUMBER, `to hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours the law asks for an escort on a free day` `from hour` `to hour` IS
    (`the working hours of an escort day` `from hour` `to hour` MINUS `the overtime of an escort day` `from hour` `to hour`)
    PLUS `regular hours section 16 asks for an escort day` `from hour` `to hour`

§§ `לינה`

-- A night away: the first day from one hour to another, the night until
-- the second day starts, and the second day. Without the night, each day
-- is its own day. With it, the night's hours come after the first day's
-- overtime, past its two hours at 125%, so §16 pays each at 150%.
GIVEN `first day from` IS A NUMBER, `first day to` IS A NUMBER, `second day from` IS A NUMBER, `second day to` IS A NUMBER
      `the night is working time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours section 16 asks for a night away` `first day from` `first day to` `second day from` `second day to` `the night is working time` IS
    `regular hours section 16 asks for an escort day` `first day from` `first day to`
    PLUS `regular hours section 16 asks for an escort day` `second day from` `second day to`
    PLUS (IF `the night is working time`
          THEN ((24 MINUS `first day to`) PLUS `second day from`) TIMES 1.5
          ELSE 0)

-- The worked night away: out at 8:00, the pupils in bed at 23:00, up at
-- 7:00, home at 17:00.
`the first day of the night away starts at` MEANS 8
`the first day of the night away ends at` MEANS 23
`the second day of the night away starts at` MEANS 7
`the second day of the night away ends at` MEANS 17

GIVEN `the night is working time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours section 16 asks for the worked night away` `the night is working time` IS
    `regular hours section 16 asks for a night away`
        `the first day of the night away starts at` `the first day of the night away ends at`
        `the second day of the night away starts at` `the second day of the night away ends at`
        `the night is working time`

§§ `השכר הרגיל לשעה`

-- Convention instruments.regular-hour-wage: the bound most generous to
-- the employer is a month of §3's longest week, 45 hours over 52 weeks.
`the most hours a month of section 3's longest week holds` MEANS
    `the longest working week section 3 allows` TIMES 52 DIVIDED BY 12

-- What activity units pay, in hours of the regular wage, when an hour is
-- the month over the given hours and a unit the given share of the month.
GIVEN units IS A NUMBER, `a unit's share of the month` IS A NUMBER, `hours of the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours activity units pay` units `a unit's share of the month` `hours of the month` IS
    units TIMES `a unit's share of the month` TIMES `hours of the month`

-- What substitution hours pay, in hours of the regular wage, when each is
-- paid at a share of an hour value that is the month over its own hours.
GIVEN `substitution hours` IS A NUMBER, `the substitution rate` IS A NUMBER, `hours the hour value divides the month by` IS A NUMBER, `hours of the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `regular hours substitution hours pay` `substitution hours` `the substitution rate` `hours the hour value divides the month by` `hours of the month` IS
    `substitution hours` TIMES `the substitution rate` TIMES `hours of the month` DIVIDED BY `hours the hour value divides the month by`

-- The law governs what pays less (§35; convention instruments.statute-floor).
GIVEN `what the law asks` IS A NUMBER, `what the instrument pays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument pays less than the Hours of Work and Rest Law asks` `what the law asks` `what the instrument pays` IF
        `what the instrument pays` LESS THAN `what the law asks`
    AND `what stands under section 35 of the Hours of Work and Rest Law` `what the law asks` `what the instrument pays` EQUALS `what the law asks`
